Add `core.bitop.isRightJustifiedOnes`

`core.bitop.isRightJustifiedOnes` checks whether the set bits of an
unsigned integer form a single, contiguous run of 1s starting at the
least significant bit (e.g. `0`, `0b0111`, `0x00FF_FFFF`). This is a
common need, but the efficient implementation is not obvious.

---
import core.bitop : isRightJustifiedOnes;

assert( isRightJustifiedOnes(0x00FF_FFFFu));
assert(!isRightJustifiedOnes(0x1010_1110u));
---
